Thank you, this is terrific work.

I was able to come up with 2 small variations that outperform this PR on my machine even without `inline(always)`.

**Variation 1:** in the Mycroft's algorithm, move `& (ONE_BYTES << 7)` and `!= 0` out of the loop. https://github.com/serde-rs/json/pull/1167

**Variation 2:** skip the memchr. Mycroft's algorithm works for finding any specific byte by xor-ing the original chunk and then testing for a zero byte. https://github.com/serde-rs/json/pull/1168

